    <cap:headline>Fishermen warning</cap:headline>
    <cap:description>Gale Wind (speed reaching 130-140 kmph gusting to 155 kmph) very likely over eastcentral Arabian Sea. It is likely to increase over eastcentral Arabian Sea becoming 145-155 kmph gusting to 170 kmph from 16th May mid-night; speed reaching 80-90 kmph gusting to 100 kmph) along and off south Maharashtra-Goa and adjoining Karnataka coasts; wind speed
reaching 50-60 kmph gusting to 70 kmph along and off north Maharashtra coast. Squally Wind (speed reaching 40-50 kmph gusting to 60 kmph) very likely over northeast Arabian Sea and along and off south Gujarat and Daman and Diu coasts. Sea conditions will be very high to phenomenal over eastcentral Arabian Sea; very rough to high along and off Maharashtra-GoaCoasts. Fis hermen are advised not to venture into these areas.</cap:description>
    <cap:instruction>Action suggested:
• Deep sea fishermen are advised to return to the coasts.</cap:instruction>
    <cap:web>http://www.rsmcnewdelhi.imd.gov.in</cap:web>
